      "prompt": "A single weathered driftwood log lying on its side on the plain grey studio floor: a bare barkless trunk section with a gently twisted spiral grain, bleached silver-grey and pale beige wood with darker grey cracks running along the grain, smooth sea-worn rounded ends, one short broken branch stub and a small splayed root flare at one end, the wood reading as a soft matte satin surface, smooth sculpted forms like a quality scale model with a bold readable silhouette, with a soft contact shadow, the whole log centred in frame and seen from the front-left. The picture shows only the driftwood log on the plain backdrop, stylized-real diorama miniature, real PBR materials, slightly exaggerated proportions, soft noon sun, neutral grey studio background"
